feat(run): default fast mode to a plain non-vector cpu, no vlen

`run --mode fast` pinned an opinionated vector core by default:
`-cpu andes-ax45mpv,vlen=512` (rv64) and `andes-d23` (rv32). Default instead
to a plain non-vector core with no vlen -- andes-ax45 (rv64), andes-a45 (rv32).
A vector run stays one flag away via the post-`--` tail
(`-- -cpu andes-ax45mpv,vlen=512`), which still wins (qemu honors the last
`-cpu`).

Only the standalone fast leg changes. The hybrid fast-leg keeps
`andes-ax45mpv,vlen={vlen}` matched to the cycle engine, because the V-state
handoff requires a vector core.

engine_registry_test updated to the new defaults; the rv32 fixture was verified
to boot live on andes-a45 via qemu-system-riscv32, and USER_GUIDE's fast-mode
default + override example were updated to match.

